.TH HIRO.CONF 5 "August 2026" "HIRO" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
hiro.conf \- HIRO daemon configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/hiro/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
TOML configuration for \fBhirod\fR(8). Every key is optional; missing
values fall back to the built-in defaults (see
.I /etc/hiro/config.toml.example
for the complete set with documentation).
.SH SECTIONS
.TP
.B [device]
Camera node selection (\fIpath\fR), IR-only enforcement (\fIrequire_ir\fR),
emitter mode, stream warm-up period.
.TP
.B [camera]
Capture geometry: \fIwidth\fR, \fIheight\fR, \fIfps\fR, \fIpixel_format\fR
(YUYV recommended), \fImax_frames\fR per attempt.
.TP
.B [recognition]
Model directory, detector/embedder names, match threshold, quorum, timeout,
liveness thresholds, and enrollment quality gates.
.TP
.B [security]
Rate limiting, lockout, per-user template limit, camera-pinning policy.
.TP
.B [storage]
Template database and encryption key paths.
.TP
.B [daemon]
Socket path, log level, audit toggle, maximum per-request timeout.
.TP
.B [keyring]
Automatic login-keyring unlock on face login. \fIenabled\fR defaults to
false; when true, \fIservices\fR lists the PAM services (e.g.
gdm-password) whose stacks receive the injected authtok. The password is
enrolled with \fBhiro keyring set\fR and re-verified against the account
before each release.
.SH RELOADING
Apply changes with:
.B hiro reload
(the daemon rebuilds the pipeline when the recognition section changes).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hirod (8),
.BR hiro (1)
